      "spice_level": "mild",
      "ingredients": [
        {
          "ingredient_name": "whole wheat flour",
          "quantity_grams": 240.0,
          "display_quantity": 2.0,
          "display_unit": "cup",
          "notes": "atta"
        },
        {
          "ingredient_name": "semolina",
          "quantity_grams": 45.0,
          "display_quantity": 0.25,
          "display_unit": "cup",
          "notes": "sooji, for crispness"
        },
        {
          "ingredient_name": "besan",
          "quantity_grams": 30.0,
          "display_quantity": 2.0,
          "display_unit": "tbsp",
          "notes": "gram flour"
        },
        {
          "ingredient_name": "ghee",
          "quantity_grams": 70.0,
          "display_quantity": 5.0,
          "display_unit": "tbsp",
          "notes": "3 tbsp for dough, 2 tbsp for coating/serving"
        },
        {
          "ingredient_name": "ajwain",
          "quantity_grams": 2.0,
          "display_quantity": 1.0,
          "display_unit": "tsp",
          "notes": "carom seeds, crushed"
        },
        {
          "ingredient_name": "salt",
          "quantity_grams": 4.0,
          "display_quantity": 0.5,
          "display_unit": "tsp",
          "notes": ""
        }
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "In a large mixing bowl, combine whole wheat flour, semolina, besan, crushed ajwain, and salt.",
        "Add 3 tablespoons of melted ghee to the flour mixture. Rub the ghee into the flour using your fingertips until it resembles coarse breadcrumbs.",
        "Gradually add warm water and knead into a stiff, tight dough (stiffer than roti dough). Let it rest for 15 minutes.",
        "Preheat your oven to 180°C (350°F) or prepare a gas tandoor.",
        "Divide the rested dough into equal lemon-sized balls. Roll them between your palms and flatten slightly, making a small indentation in the center with your thumb.",
        "Place the baatis on a baking tray. Bake for 30-40 minutes, flipping them halfway, until they are golden brown and cooked from the inside with visible cracks.",
        "Once baked, lightly crush each hot baati to open it up slightly.",
        "Drizzle generously with the remaining ghee (or dip them in melted ghee). Serve immediately with Panchmel Dal."
      ]
